  "visualInspection": [
    "The long low orange carrier, front blue-glass driver cab and smaller offset glazed operator pod read as a mobile crane with its equipment stowed. The three broad yellow boom sections create a restrained stepped longitudinal silhouette rather than a tall raised crane.",
    "Actual fixed gray tip shoe, short dark cable and small gray J hook sit near the front stowed tip. Their physical surfaces and separate paint ownership are verified by actual triangle rays; their small profile naturally becomes thin or occluded in end-on headings.",
    "Four short retracted yellow caps with dark outer end faces remain tucked into the carrier sides. No extended stabilizer arms or ground feet are presented; actual four-cap positions and fixed width are verified independently.",
    "Driver and operator glass/frames belong to separate actual body-skin charts. The visible carrier-front skin owns the silver grille; there are no transparent glazing sheets, PBR materials, glass overlay intersections, text or logos.",
    "All three near-side axles remain grounded with silver hubs beneath integrated orange arches. Far crowns remain under real hull/fender surfaces in both camera families; no floating cap-only cover or exposed crown spill was observed.",
    "All6 independent quarter/reverse/pivot/absolute-reset controls pass while cab, hull, pod, boom, hook, cable and four caps remain fixed. Signed phases and both actual wireframes were inspected. No working equipment motion node is present.",
    "All32 native256/radius128 views have zero border pixels. Centered128 game crop parity is exact at all16 headings. All4 cardinals fit standard192x224 origin96,144 by integer translation(-32,+16), preserving every occupiedRGBA pixel.",
    "Broad orange/yellow paint clusters remain readable at native density. Thin cab frames, stepped boom edges and small cable/hook retain ordinary native-pixel aliasing. Equipment stow proofs qualify this single fixed pose only; no lift/telescope/cable/outrigger animation or gameplay is claimed."
  ],
